      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While box breathing can be a highly effective tool for managing stress, it's not a one-size-fits-all solution. Overextensive use can lead to relaxation fatigue, a phenomenon where prolonged activation of the parasympathetic nervous system can actually impair performance and reduce alertness. Additionally, if used when trying to focus intensely, such as during critical tasks, it may interfere with the body's \"fight or flight\" response, potentially hindering concentration and performance.",
